      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hilltop Lakes, an upscale community off Farm Road 3, sits about 18 miles southwest of Centerville in southwestern Leon County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/hilltop-lakes-tx",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community centers around five man‑made lakes—Mirror, Swan, Kickapoo, Cherokee, and Lake Tonkawa—created for residents’ recreation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilltop_Lakes%2C_Texas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Those lakes sit on Running Creek or its tributary, which flows south into the Navasota River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilltop_Lakes%2C_Texas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Resort development in Hilltop Lakes began in the mid‑1960s, shaping its modern upscale character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/hilltop-lakes-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Swan Lake and Lake Tonkawa, two of the community’s man‑made lakes, were early focal points for boating and fishing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
